# Phase 5.1 — Exotel Outbound Calling

## Phase Gate Confirmation

Phase 4 (`PHASE_4_INTEGRATION.md`) is marked **DONE** in `PHASE_PROGRESS.md`. Phase 5.1 is eligible to start.

## Objective

Build the Exotel outbound calling client and webhook endpoint so the server can trigger outgoing telephone calls and correctly handle the applet callback that routes call audio into our WebSocket transport.

---

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> **Webhook response format discrepancy.** The `PHASE_5_1_OUTBOUND.md` spec says the webhook should return **ExoML XML** (`<Response><Connect><Stream url="wss://..."/></Connect></Response>`). However, research confirms that Exotel's **Voicebot Applet** (the bidirectional streaming applet used with Pipecat) uses a **different pattern**: Exotel sends a `GET` request to your webhook URL, and your server must return a **JSON response** with `{"url": "wss://..."}`.
>
> The ExoML `<Connect><Stream>` pattern is for the **Stream Applet** (unidirectional). Since our architecture uses **bidirectional audio** (Voicebot Applet), we should use the JSON response format instead.
>
> **Proposed correction:** The webhook at `GET /telephony/webhook` will return `JSONResponse({"url": "wss://{PUBLIC_NGROK_URL}/telephony/exotel"})` instead of XML.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Exotel cluster subdomain.** Exotel has two API clusters:
> - **Mumbai Cluster:** `api.in.exotel.com` (dashboard: `my.in.exotel.com`)
> - **Singapore Cluster:** `api.exotel.com` (dashboard: `my.exotel.com`)
>
> The PHASE_5_1 spec lists 6 env vars but does not include `EXOTEL_SUBDOMAIN`. I propose adding it as a 7th config field with a default of `api.exotel.com`, since the correct cluster depends on which Exotel dashboard the user's account is registered on.

